--   Tables for the finite Rosser--Schoenfeld $\theta$ certificate
-- statement:
--   Data tables used by a machine-checked certificate for Rosser--Schoenfeld's finite-range lower bound $t - 2\sqrt t < \theta(t)$ on $255 \le t \le 1420$ (Theorem 19, 1962). The table `clbZ` stores, for each prime $p \le 1420$, the value $\lfloor 10^4 \log p \rfloor$ (and $0$ off the primes); `plist` is the explicit finet of primes $\le 1420$, presented as the union of four consecutive chunks `plist1`--`plist4`; and `blocks` is the explicit interval cover of $[255,1420]$ by 71 intervals (in four consecutive chunks `blk1`--`blk4`) on which the lower bound is checked.
-- source:
--   J.B. Rosser, L. Schoenfeld, Approximate formulas for some functions of prime numbers, Illinois J. Math. 6 (1962), 64-94; p. 82, Theorem 19 (finite window), used in the '288' chain of the Lemma 15 proof, p. 89. https://doi.org/10.1215/ijm/1255631807

import Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic
import Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Nat

/-!
# Tables for the finite Rosser--Schoenfeld theta certificate

Data used by the machine-checked certificate for
`t - 2*sqrt t < theta t` on `255 <= t <= 1420`
(Rosser--Schoenfeld 1962, Theorem 19, finite window):

* `clbZ p` -- the 4-decimal floor of `log p` scaled by `10^4`, for primes `p <= 1420`;
* `plist` -- the primes `<= 1420`, split into four consecutive chunks
  `plist1, plist2, plist3, plist4`;
* `blocks` -- the interval cover of `[255, 1420]` used by the certificate,
  split into four consecutive chunks `blk1, blk2, blk3, blk4`.
-/

namespace TaoFivePrimes

open Finset

